      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Optical detection and coherent control of solid-state spins made single defects in diamond useful as quantum systems and sensitive probes, creating an important bridge between quantum optics, materials, and sensing.",
        "attribution": "Jelezko and Wrachtrup established key experimental capabilities with nitrogen-vacancy centres, while Lukin helped develop the quantum-control and sensing vision. The field draws on contributions from a broad community.",
        "maturity": "The core methods have been independently demonstrated and developed over many years. Some proposed sensing applications are still being assessed against practical limits.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "It remains difficult to distinguish the foundational discovery of controllable defects from the expanding set of quantum sensing applications."
        ]
      }
    }
